{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548241-clans-bloodlines-that-you-have-a-soft-spot-for","id":1548241,"title":"Clans/Bloodlines that you have a soft spot for?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-05T17:10:05-08:00","id":1548241,"title":"Clans/Bloodlines that you have a soft spot for?","content":"Which groups do you like but haven't really used lots but still find interesting?<br /> <br /> Mine are the Brujah and Nagaraja lineage.<br /> <br /> The Brujah appeal to my more rebellious side and can't seem to acknowledge that kindred and humanity living in harmony is impossible and the Nagaraja image of creepy and possibly demented necromancers with no clear founder for some reason intrigued me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T21:17:45-08:00","id":1548245,"title":"","content":"The Salubri. Either in their historical version of healer caste trying to be good and moral despite everything or the warrior caste smiting Baali, or in the Antribu version where they are blood mad crusaders spitting on everything Samiel and Saulot stood for the chance of revenge against their clan's murderers. <br /> <br /> They also have a mark on them that shows they are otherworldly and no longer human and doesn't require potentially centuries to show up like the cappadocians or Assamites. Plus I think the third eye looks cool. I also like their discipline","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T22:44:36-08:00","id":1548246,"title":"","content":"I should add that I also have a soft spot for Old Clan Tziscme even if I will never really use them as a character or even as a npc. There dislike for the parent clan and flesh crafting in general and still being much of the same mindset in general. The Tziscme is the only High Clan I really appreciate the most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T22:45:39-08:00","id":1548247,"title":"","content":"Of course as you can see by my tag that I love the Followers of Set/Ministry and Malkavian clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T15:06:22-08:00","id":1548269,"title":"","content":"VDA20 Setites, with the three bloodlines: Warriors of Glycon, Priests (of Set? Would this be their full name?), Witches of Echidna.<br /> <br /> But I have fancied many clans and bloodlines through the years. Assamites (all three castes) and Malkavians stand out in my memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T16:46:14-08:00","id":1548277,"title":"","content":"My tastes have stayed consistent with the Followers of Set/Ministry, Gangrel, Malkavian, Ravnos and Tziscme clans.<br /> <br /> But I have gained a appreciation for the Ventrue from the Dark Ages, but not enough to ever play one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T18:26:44-08:00","id":1548283,"title":"","content":"I like the Giovanni as I find them to be a superior choice for a Necromancer Clan above the Cappadocians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-15T05:50:01-08:00","id":1548512,"title":"","content":"Brujah, Toreador, Tremere, Ravnos, and Giovanni","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-16T16:31:39-08:00","id":1548541,"title":"","content":"Setite and Brujah<br /> <br /> Brujah appeals to me because i have anger issues. I can identify with the struggle, and i really like politics. I dont like how it end up in harmful stereotypes of having anger issues, and the whole &quot;Rebel without cause&quot; aesthethic schitck is just boring, but in the end, i identify with them<br /> <br /> Setite because i like the Clanbook Followers of Setite Revised, even if it has some... distateful decitions. Even if their theology ends up being basic Gnosticism, i like how it subverts how setites are represented, and the Ministries are just... *Chef Kiss*<br /> <br /> In bloodlines side, i like Salubries. Maybe because im catholic, but Saulot best Antediluvian and all that &quot;MUH SAULOT CREATED THE BAALI&quot; is just nihilist crap. You cant have a grim world without hope. You cant have evil if you dont have goodness to contrast it. And Salubries are the contrast. They are the &quot;Good vampire&quot;. When others vampires fucks about how they are cursed and that makes them do shit, the Salubries are there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28021-camaradadoppio","name":"CamaradaDoppio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28021_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-17T10:27:01-08:00","id":1548555,"title":"","content":"I absolutely love the True Brujah. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T05:46:44-08:00","id":1548583,"title":"","content":"I like the Setites, Witches of Echidna are my jam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-26T10:34:05-08:00","id":1548792,"title":"","content":"Among the clans, I'm quite fond of all of them. Maybe Tzimisce or Lasombra mostly, since I like to play Sabbat games.<br /> <br /> Harbingers of Skulls are probably my favourite bloodline (and are probably preferred over the clans, too), but that'll probably change tomorrow. I also like the following more or less, depending on my mood:<ul><li>Baali (VTDA Clanbook version only)</li> <li>Nagaraja</li> <li>Lamia</li> <li>Ahrimanes</li> <li>Salubri <i>antitribu</i></li> <li>Gargoyles (or, at least, the one in <i>Montreal by Night</i>, who I imagine founded a new bloodline)</li> </ul>But what I like about VTM is how reading a bloodline (or clan) description always makes me want to play one of them right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T17:45:28-08:00","id":1549038,"title":"","content":"The Ventrue of the Dark Ages I gained a appreciation for being the underdogs in Kindred society when the Lasombra seemed to be the top clan in terms of political power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-14T23:21:57-07:00","id":1549332,"title":"","content":"Cappadocians. Still feels like they've been done dirty in 5e, seemingly totally subsumed by the Harbingers. About 5 years ago I posted a homebrew Cappadocian Hecata bloodline. It was controversial since I gave them Presence due to their rage (even got a writers response).<br /> <br /> -edit- found it:<br /> <br /> Cappadocian (Hecata)<br /> Optional Discipline Spread: Fortitude, Oblivion, Presence<br /> <br /> The Cappadocian's... countless were sacrificed by our founder, then we were almost exterminated by the treacherous Giovanni, and finally nearly subsumed by the wraith's called Harbingers. The true Clan of Death has returned. The Promise of 1528 has not been forgotten. The Cappadocian's will not be forgotten!<br /> <br /> Bloodline Abilities<br /> 1- Unliving Resolve: The Cappadocian's have endured, and will always endure, once per scene add one automatic success to any Stamina or Resolve Roll.<br /> <br /> 2- Necromantic Adept: The Cappadocian's have studied death for countless millennia, gain two extra die on any Oblivion Ceremony roll relating to raising the dead and animated dead add two extra die to resist disintegration.<br /> <br /> 3- Fear of Oblivion: The Cappadocian's channel the fury of their lost clan, getting two extra die on any Intimidation roll against Hecata and also causing a two dice penalty on any Social roll from Hecata that is targeting the Cappadocian.<br /> <br /> 4- Crypt Guard: The Cappadocian's have learned many practical lessons in securing rest, gain four dots to spread between Haven and Retainers.<br /> <br /> 5- Awaken: The Cappadocian's have rediscovered an ancient rite, with it they can attempt to raise themselves or another Kindred from Torpor. Spend two points of Willpower and Roll Resolve + Medicine (difficulty 10 - Humanity) for one turn each success you awaken yourself or another Kindred, but suffering from Hunger 5. Reducing Hunger to 4 or less fully awakens the Kindred. Until fully awakened the Kindred is more an animated corpse and as such may act even while staked (fire and sunlight are unaffected).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26215,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","user":"Kahnabys","date":". 03-15-2025, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26215-kahnabys","name":"Kahnabys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T03:39:53-07:00","id":1549497,"title":"","content":"I do quite like the Cappadocians. Though, I gotta admit, the Harbingers are more appealing in a VTM game\u2014they can encompass the contemplative, studious types, but they also have that violent, unhinged contingent that makes them more active players in the Modern (or Final) Nights.<br /> <br /> With the surviving &quot;true&quot; Cappaodcians being a fragmented bunch of isolationists, they're about on a par with the (non-Sabbat) Salubri in terms of rarity and vulnerability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T04:42:59-07:00","id":1549726,"title":"","content":"Tbh, I just don't like the Hecata in V5. Throwing all the vaguely necromantic-themed clans into a dull vaguely witchy slop is just disheartening.<br /> <br /> Bring back the old-school Giovanni (or Cappadocians if you're playing Dark Ages)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T15:11:52-07:00","id":1549751,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the Hecate, but I can see why people not liking the idea of having the various lineages becoming one clan when some of them have bad blood between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T18:59:12-07:00","id":1549762,"title":"","content":"I think that the Hecata would have been a good idea if that had been the original Clan and then the Giovanni, Cappadocians, Harbingers, and Samedi could have been Bloodlines or even just factions with the Clan.<br /> <br /> Having those various Bloodlines join together when they are natural enemies is more of a problem to me. Also, it creates a sort of Necromancer Sect, which kind of destroys player options compared to having those various Necromancer Bloodlines joining different Sects and then someone can play a Necromancer regardless of the Sect that the chronicle focuses on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 04-02-2025, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}